Waive weapon, positioning and reagent requirements on player casts.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp

Why: player report -- "can we ignore item requirements for attacks like that
(and positioning like behind target for that matter) AND also remove reagent
requirements from spells/buffs that players cast?"

"Attacks like that" is Hemorrhage's spread. Bug #23/#28 was a rogue watching
the spread hook fire (13 casts logged) while nothing landed, because Ambush
is dagger-only and Hemorrhage is explicitly not-a-dagger; the two can never
be satisfied at once. Adding TRIGGERED_IGNORE_EQUIPPED_ITEM_REQUIREMENT to
that one call site fixed that one spread. This generalises it, because the
same class of rule was going to keep producing the same class of report --
Backstab wanting a dagger, and behind-the-target wanting a melee dance that
mostly punishes latency.

Three sites, all in Spell::CheckCast / Spell::CheckItems:

  SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM_CLASS   weapon class/subclass requirement
  SPELL_FAILED_NOT_BEHIND            SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_CASTER_BEHIND_TARGET
  SPELL_FAILED_NOT_INFRONT           SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_TARGET_FACING_CASTER
  checkReagents                      spell component consumption

Scope: players only. Every site tests IsPlayer() (the reagent block is
already inside a player-only branch) so creature casts keep every check.
That matters for the equipped-item test in particular: for a creature that
check is how being disarmed works, and it is a real mechanic worth keeping.

Reagents were already half-waived. Core-patch 0011 tops the player's bag up
from the reagent vault during CheckCast, which had made "do you physically
hold it" the wrong question for anything the vault stocked. This finishes
that: the check does not run for players, so nothing is demanded.

CRAFTING IS EXCLUDED, and this is the part worth reading twice. Every
profession spell lists its materials as reagents -- there is no separate
"materials" system -- so a blanket waiver does not remove an errand, it lets
anyone produce Titansteel Bars from an empty bag and deletes the crafting
economy in one line. LivingGear_SpellPaysReagents() keeps the cost on
anything that manufactures or alters an item:

  CREATE_ITEM / CREATE_ITEM_2 / CREATE_RANDOM_ITEM
  ENCHANT_ITEM / _TEMPORARY / _PRISMATIC / ENCHANT_HELD_ITEM
  TRADE_SKILL, DISENCHANT, PROSPECTING, MILLING

Spell::TakeReagents carries the same test. It has to: consumption is a
separate function from the check, so waiving only the check would destroy
the component of a player who happened to be carrying one while a player
with an empty bag cast for free -- punishing precisely the person who
prepared. Both sides move together or neither does.

Gated by LivingGear.IgnoreSpellRequirements (default 1), read via
LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements() in LivingGear_Perks.cpp.

Not covered: totem requirements, spell focus objects (anvil, forge), and
SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM (a specific required item, as opposed to a weapon
class). Those are the checks where the requirement is the point of the spell
rather than a tax on it. Revisit if a report says otherwise.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ near the other Living Gear forward declarations
+bool LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements();
+
+static bool LivingGear_SpellPaysReagents(SpellInfo const* spellInfo)
+{
+    // true for anything that manufactures or alters an item -- see above
+}

@@ Spell::TakeReagents, after the CanNoReagentCast bail
+    if (LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements() && !LivingGear_SpellPaysReagents(m_spellInfo))
+        return;

@@ Spell::CheckCast, the facing checks
+            bool const bonesawIgnorePositioning =
+                LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements() && m_caster->IsPlayer();
+
     // Must be behind the target
-    if (m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_CASTER_BEHIND_TARGET) && ...)
+    if (!bonesawIgnorePositioning
+        && m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_CASTER_BEHIND_TARGET) && ...)
         return SPELL_FAILED_NOT_BEHIND;
     // Target must be facing you
-    if (m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_TARGET_FACING_CASTER) && ...)
+    if (!bonesawIgnorePositioning
+        && m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_CU_REQ_TARGET_FACING_CASTER) && ...)
         return SPELL_FAILED_NOT_INFRONT;

@@ Spell::CheckItems, the weapon requirement
-    if (m_caster->IsPlayer() && !m_caster->ToPlayer()->HasItemFitToSpellRequirements(m_spellInfo))
+    if (!LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements() && m_caster->IsPlayer()
+        && !m_caster->ToPlayer()->HasItemFitToSpellRequirements(m_spellInfo))
         return SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM_CLASS;

@@ Spell::CheckItems, the reagent gate
-    bool checkReagents = !HasTriggeredCastFlag(TRIGGERED_IGNORE_POWER_AND_REAGENT_COST) && !player->CanNoReagentCast(m_spellInfo);
+    bool checkReagents = !LivingGear_IgnoreSpellRequirements()
+        && !HasTriggeredCastFlag(TRIGGERED_IGNORE_POWER_AND_REAGENT_COST)
+        && !player->CanNoReagentCast(m_spellInfo);
